/---------------------------------------------
/This program take an input string from user,
/Output the string scrolling it horizontally
/each time a character shift position, screen goes to a darker shade of blue,
/then goes back to while, before continuing iterating throug shade of blue again,
/until the whole string has been shown on screen 
/recomended input to get a full iteration of the shades: Monashgood#


/ --- MAIN PROGRAM ---
Load StringAddr
Store StringAddrForPainting
JnS SubPaintString

/ This is the end of the main program.
Halt

/NOTE: {comments structure}
/ --- [comment] ---   | this is brief decsription of what the next block of code do
/ [comment]           | This is individual line of code comment or more indepth description of what the code block 
/ --------------------------------  | Subroutine separation

/ --- constant used through the program; ---
STARTDISP,      HEX 0F00
COUNT256,       DEC 256
THIRTYTWO,      DEC 32
TWELVE,         DEC 12
EIGHT,          DEC 8
FOUR,           DEC 4
TWO,            DEC 2
ONE,            DEC 1

ASCII_A,        HEX 041
ASCII_Z,        HEX 05A
ASCII_a,        HEX 061
ASCII_z,        HEX 07A
DELAYCONST,     DEC 2500   

DisplayLEFT, HEX 0F51 
DisplayMID, HEX 0F56
DisplayRIGHT, HEX 0f5B


/------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ --- This subroutine sets F00 to FFF(I.e., the screen) to shade of blue ---
SubClearDisplay,   HEX 0

		    /PTR1 = STARTDISP
		    Load    STARTDISP
		    Store   PTR1
		
		    /COUNT = 256 Pixels
		    Load    COUNT256
		    Store   COUNT

			
			/Iterates between shades of blue
			/goes from light blue to dark blue to white and back to light blue 
            /Note: colour change occure everytime function ClearDisplay is called
			Load    colour        
            subt    colourchange     
			store   colour      

/ --- Iterates though every pixel of the screen and change it to the current colour ---
CD_Loop,    load    colour
		    StoreI  PTR1
		
		    Load    PTR1                  /PTR1 incremented by 1
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   PTR1
		
		    Load    COUNT                 /COUNT decremented by 1 
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   COUNT
		
		    Load    COUNT                 /if COUNT != 0, loop
		    SkipCond 400                  /skip next if AC == 0
		    Jump    CD_Loop

            JumpI   SubClearDisplay

PTR1,           HEX 0     /store the screen pixel memory address.
COUNT,          HEX 0     /Counts up to 256; all pixel for the screen
colour,         hex FFFF  /stores the screen colour, initially set to white
colourchange,   hex 1000  /store the value that will produce the blue shade shift.

/------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ --- Subroutine to input a string ---
InputStringAddr,   HEX 0
SubInputString,    Hex 0 

/ --- read one character from keyboard and save character in SI_CHAR ---
ReadLoop,       Input                     
			    Store   SI_CHAR           
	
/ --- Check if character is uppercase (A..Z) ---
			    Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    ASCII_A
			    SkipCond 000              /skip next if char < 'A'
			    Jump    CapHighCheck
			    Jump    StoreDelimiter    /if < 'A', not alphabetic → delimiter

CapHighCheck,   Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    ASCII_Z
			    SkipCond 800              /skip next if char > 'Z'
			    Jump    StoreAlphabet     /in range A..Z
			    Jump    CheckLower        /else maybe lowercase

/ --- Check if character is lowercase (a..z) ---
CheckLower,     Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    ASCII_a
			    SkipCond 000              /skip next if char < 'a'
			    Jump    LowerHighCheck
			    Jump    StoreDelimiter    /if < 'a', not alphabetic

LowerHighCheck,	Load    SI_CHAR
				Subt    ASCII_z
				SkipCond 800              /skip next if char > 'z'
				Jump    ConvertToUpper    /valid lowercase
				Jump    StoreDelimiter    /not alphabetic

/ --- Convert lowercase to uppercase ---
ConvertToUpper, Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    THIRTYTWO         /ASCII offset between 'a' and 'A'
			    Store   SI_CHAR
			    Jump    StoreAlphabet

/ --- Store the alphabetic character ---
StoreAlphabet,  Load    SI_CHAR
			    StoreI  InputStringAddr   /write character into string
			
			    Load    InputStringAddr
			    Add     ONE               /move pointer forward
			    Store   InputStringAddr
			
			    Jump    ReadLoop          / read next character

/ --- Store delimiter and terminate subroutine ---
StoreDelimiter, Load    SI_CHAR
			    StoreI  InputStringAddr   / store the delimiter
			    JumpI   SubInputString    / return to caller
				
/ --- Variables for the subroutine subInputstring ---    
SI_CHAR,   HEX 0   


/------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ This subroutine paints a character on the display
PaintCharCharacter, HEX 0
PaintCharDisplay, HEX 0  

SubPaintChar, HEX 0 

            
		    / --- Set row counter = 8 ---
		    Load    EIGHT
		    Store   PC_RowCnt

RowLoop,    Load    FOUR                  / Reset column counter = 4
            Store   PC_ColCnt

ColLoop,    LoadI   PaintCharCharacter    / Copy one pixel from character to print -> display
            SkipCond 400
			load    colour
		    StoreI  PaintCharDisplay
		
		    / --- Advance character pixel ---
		    Load    PaintCharCharacter
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   PaintCharCharacter
		
		    / --- Advance display pixel ---
		    Load    PaintCharDisplay
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   PaintCharDisplay
		
		    / --- Decrement column counter ---
		    Load    PC_ColCnt
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   PC_ColCnt
		
		    / --- Loop until 4 pixels written ---
		    Load    PC_ColCnt
		    SkipCond 400                  / skip next if 0
		    Jump    ColLoop
		
		    / --- Finished one row of 4 -> skip ahead 12 in display ---
		    Load    PaintCharDisplay
		    Add     TWELVE
		    Store   PaintCharDisplay
		
		    / --- Decrement row counter ---
		    Load    PC_RowCnt
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   PC_RowCnt
		
		    / --- Loop until 8 rows done ---
		    Load    PC_RowCnt
		    SkipCond 400                  / skip if 0
		    Jump    RowLoop
		
		    JumpI   SubPaintChar

/ --- Variables for the subroutine SubPaintChar ---  
PC_RowCnt,    HEX 0                       / number of rows (8)
PC_ColCnt,    HEX 0                       / number of columns (4)


/--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ --- Subroutine to paint horizontally scrolling text on screen ---
StringAddrForPainting, HEX 0
SubPaintString,        HEX 0

/ --- Take the user input string ---
Load StringAddr
Store InputStringAddr
JnS SubInputString


/ --- get the next 3 character to display on screen ---
NextCharLoop,   LoadI StringAddrForPainting
			    Store PS_CHAR                 / get left most character to display on screen
				
			    load StringAddrForPainting
			    add ONE
			    store temp
			    LoadI temp
			    store PS_NEXT_CHAR            /get middle character to display on screen


				Load StringAddrForPainting   
				add TWO
				store temp
				LoadI temp
				Store PS_NEXT_NEXT_CHAR         /get right most character to display on screen

				/ --- check if the right most character is an alphabetical character ---
				/ --- if it is indeed an alphabetical character, proceed with program
				/ --- else program stops ---
				subt ASCII_A
				SkipCond 000              / If char < A ->stop
				Jump CHECKALPHA
				JUMP EndPaintString
CHECKALPHA,     load PS_NEXT_NEXT_CHAR
				Subt ASCII_Z
				SkipCond 800              / IF char > Z -> STOP
				JUMP DoChar1			
			    Jump EndPaintString


/ --- DoChar1, DoChar2, DoChar3 ---
/ --- prints the character on screen ---
/ --- 3 characters are shown on screen at a time ---
/ --- for next iteration, each character moves to the left;
/ --- I.e., middle character goes to left most character position, 
/ --- right most character goes to middle character position,
/ --- next character in string take left most character position.

DoChar1,JnS SubClearDisplay     
        Load    PS_CHAR  
		Subt    ASCII_A                  
		Store   PS_INDEX
	
	    / --- Multiply index × 32 inline ---
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×2
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×4
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×8
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×16
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×32
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    FontAddr
		Store  PaintCharCharacter         
	
	    / --- Set display address to leftmost charatcer position ---
		Load    DisplayLEFT                / Use DisplayLEFT to display character in the middle left of screen
		Store   PaintCharDisplay
	
	    / --- Paint char using subroutine subpaintchar ---
		JnS     SubPaintChar


DoChar2,Load    PS_NEXT_CHAR  
		Subt    ASCII_A                   
		Store   PS_INDEX
	
	    / --- Multiply index × 32 inline ---
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×2
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×4
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×8
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×16
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×32
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    FontAddr
		Store  PaintCharCharacter         
	
	    / --- Set display address to middle character position ---
		Load    DisplayMID               /Use DisplayMID to display character in the middle of screen

		Store   PaintCharDisplay
	
	    / --- Paint char using subroutine subpaintchar ---
		JnS     SubPaintChar


DoChar3,Load    PS_NEXT_NEXT_CHAR  
		Subt    ASCII_A                   
		Store   PS_INDEX
	
	    / --- Multiply index × 32 inline ---
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×2
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×4
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×8
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×16
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×32
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    FontAddr
		Store  PaintCharCharacter        
	
	    / --- Set display address to rightmost character position ---
		Load    DisplayRIGHT               / Use DisplayRIGHT to display character in the middle right of screen

		Store   PaintCharDisplay
	
	    / --- Paint char using subroutine subpaintchar ---
		JnS     SubPaintChar


	    / --- Delay variable ---
		Load    DELAYCONST
		Store   PS_DELAY

/ --- delay loop, make the system iterate though a loop; this makes the system waits for till the looping is done
DelayLoop,  Load    PS_DELAY
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   PS_DELAY
		    SkipCond 400
		    Jump    DelayLoop

		    / --- Advance pointer to next character ---
		    Load    StringAddrForPainting
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   StringAddrForPainting
		    Jump    NextCharLoop

EndPaintString, JumpI   SubPaintString

/ --- Variables for the subroutine SubPaintString --- 
PS_INDEX,  HEX 0
PS_CHAR,   HEX 0
PS_DELAY,  HEX 0

PS_NEXT_CHAR, HEX 0
PS_NEXT_NEXT_CHAR, HEX 0
temp, hex 0

/--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ This is the "font", the memory that stores character data for the display.
/ The characters are stored in the order A-Z.
/ Each character is 4 pixels wide and 8 pixels high.
/ The data for each character is stored row by row, with each pixel
/ being represented as ONE word that is either FFFF (white) or 0000 (black).

FontAddr, ADR FontStart
FontStart, 	HEX FFFF  / Start of character A 
			HEX 0000
			HEX 0000
